2. COMMERCIAL EVALUATION: FULLY FUNCTIONAL 40-DAY TRIAL
================================================================================

2.1. Evaluation Grant.
     Licensor grants each Commercial Entity a non-exclusive,
     non-transferable license to install and use the fully functional
     Evaluation Version for forty (40) consecutive calendar days solely
     to evaluate its suitability for that entity's internal requirements.

     Reasonable internal pilot use is permitted for evaluation. The
     evaluation license does not authorize resale, public hosting, or
     provision of the Software as a service to third parties.

2.2. Beginning and Scope of Evaluation.
     The evaluation period begins on the date of the first installation
     for that Commercial Entity, including installation by an employee or
     contractor acting on its behalf. The period applies to the entity,
     not separately to each user, device, department, or office.

     Prior use solely under Section 3 does not consume a later commercial
     evaluation period; in that case, the period begins when Commercial
     Use first occurs.

2.3. No Restart or Extension by Technical Means.
     Reinstallation, upgrades, replacement devices, new accounts, virtual
     machines, snapshots, or changes to system clocks do not restart or
     extend the evaluation period. Only Licensor may authorize an
     extension or an additional evaluation, in writing.

2.4. Purchase or Discontinue.
     Before continuing Commercial Use after the evaluation period,
     Licensee must purchase sufficient commercial license coverage for
     its deployment. Otherwise, Licensee must cease Commercial Use and
     remove the Software from commercially deployed devices and images.

     Copies used exclusively under Section 3 may be retained. An
     inaccessible backup may remain until deleted in the ordinary backup
     cycle, provided it is not restored for unauthorized use.

2.5. No Implied Extension.
     Continued operation of the Software, absence of a reminder, or lack
     of technical enforcement does not extend the evaluation license.
     Unauthorized use is a breach of this Agreement and may also
     constitute infringement under applicable law.

     The evaluation does not automatically convert into a paid
     subscription, and no purchase obligation arises merely from
     evaluating and timely discontinuing the Software.

