4. COMMERCIAL LICENSE TIERS
================================================================================

4.1. General Commercial Grant.
     Upon payment of the applicable fees, Licensor grants Licensee a
     non-exclusive license to install and use the Registered Version
     for Licensee's internal business purposes within the purchased
     scope. Transfer and sublicensing are prohibited except as required
     by mandatory law or expressly authorized by Licensor.

4.2. Single-User Commercial License.
     This license covers one designated, named individual and permits
     installation on up to two (2) physical or virtual computing
     devices used by that individual.

     The devices may not be used to provide access to unlicensed users.
     A shared workstation does not replace the named-user requirement.
     An employee or contractor may be the designated user.

4.3. Multi-User Volume Corporate License.
     This license covers the quantity and licensing metric specified
     in the Order.

     Unless the Order expressly provides otherwise, the metric is
     named users, each with the two-device allowance in Section 4.2.
     Device-based, endpoint-based, or concurrent-user licensing applies
     only if expressly stated in the Order.

     Named-user licenses may not be pooled among rotating users.
     A concurrent-user license, if expressly granted, limits simultaneous
     access rather than total installations.

4.4. Enterprise Worldwide Site License.
     This license permits deployment without a numerical user or device
     limit across Licensee's worldwide operations and any Affiliates
     expressly covered by the Order, subject to stated scope restrictions.

     Covered deployments may include offices, remote employees,
     workstations, virtual desktops, and Licensee-controlled hosted
     infrastructure. Contractors may use the Software solely to perform
     work for covered entities.

     This license does not cover customers, unrelated third parties,
     public software-as-a-service offerings, or Affiliates not included
     in the Order. Newly acquired entities are included only if the
     Order expressly provides for them or Licensor confirms inclusion
     in writing.

4.5. Reassignment and Device Replacement.
     Licensee may replace licensed devices and permanently reassign
     named-user licenses when personnel or responsibilities change,
     provided the former user or device ceases licensed use. Reassignment
     may not be used to simulate floating or concurrent licensing.

4.6. Term and Version Coverage.
     Unless the Order expressly specifies a subscription or fixed term,
     commercial licenses are perpetual for the release identified in
     the Order or, if none is identified, the current release supplied
     at purchase.

     Future releases, major upgrades, maintenance, and support are
     included only to the extent stated in the Order or expressly
     designated by Licensor as included in that entitlement.

4.7. Deployment Copies.
     Licensee may make reasonable backup and deployment copies within
     its licensed scope. A dormant backup or installation image does
     not itself require an additional license, but its deployment or
     execution must be covered.

