9. BYOM ARCHITECTURE, PRIVACY, AND DATA HANDLING
================================================================================

9.1. Bring Your Own Model.
     NativeLingo is an independent client application that communicates
     with a model endpoint selected and configured by Licensee. Endpoints
     may include third-party cloud APIs or local inference servers such
     as Ollama or LM Studio.

9.2. No Telemetry or Data Harvesting.
     The official Software contains no built-in behavioral tracking,
     background telemetry, analytics collection, or data-harvesting
     functionality. User content is not routed through a Licensor-operated
     intermediary or proxy.

     Through the Software, Licensor does not intercept, receive, inspect,
     collect, retain, or store Licensee's clipboard text, translation
     prompts, or outputs.

     Local application access to clipboard text for a user-requested
     operation is not access by Licensor.

9.3. Local and Air-Gapped Operation.
     When configured exclusively to use a local model endpoint, the
     Software sends processing requests to that endpoint rather than
     to a cloud model provider.

     A 100 percent air-gapped deployment requires Licensee to operate
     the Software, model server, and supporting systems entirely within
     an isolated environment with no external network path. In that
     configuration, Software-directed content processing remains inside
     that environment.

     Merely selecting Ollama, LM Studio, or another local-model product
     does not establish an air gap or guarantee absolute confidentiality.
     Third-party logging, plugins, cloud synchronization, backups,
     operating-system behavior, malware, and endpoint configuration
     remain outside Licensor's control. No representation is made that
     processing occurs only in volatile memory or that third-party
     software never writes data to disk.

9.4. Cloud Endpoints.
     If Licensee selects a cloud or externally hosted endpoint, relevant
     prompts, text, and request data are transmitted to that endpoint.
     Its operator's terms, retention policies, security measures, and
     international transfer arrangements apply.

9.5. API Accounts and Credentials.
     Licensee is responsible for obtaining authorized models, accounts,
     API keys, and necessary permissions, paying provider charges, and
     safeguarding credentials. Commercial NativeLingo licenses do not
     include model subscriptions, API credits, or inference services.

9.6. Licensee Responsibilities.
     Licensee controls endpoint selection, network access, model-server
     settings, content submitted, and authorization to process that
     content. Licensee must assess whether its configuration satisfies
     applicable confidentiality, privacy, and security obligations.

9.7. Administrative Communications.
     Information voluntarily supplied when purchasing a license,
     requesting support, or contacting Licensor is separate from
     in-application content processing. Licensor may handle that
     information as necessary to fulfill the request, administer the
     license, and comply with applicable law. Do not submit confidential
     prompts, documents, or API secrets through public support channels.

