13. TERM AND TERMINATION
================================================================================

13.1. This Agreement takes effect upon valid acceptance and continues for
      the applicable license term unless terminated under this Section.
      Evaluation rights expire automatically as provided in Section 2.

13.2. Licensee may terminate its rights at any time by ceasing use and
      deleting the relevant Software copies and registration materials.
      Voluntary termination does not create a refund right except as
      required by law or expressly agreed.

13.3. Licensor may terminate an affected license for a material breach
      not remedied within fifteen (15) calendar days after written notice.
      Licensor may terminate immediately by written notice for deliberate
      licensing circumvention, unauthorized sale or public disclosure of
      registration credentials, or a material breach incapable of remedy.

13.4. Upon termination or expiration, Licensee must cease use under the
      affected entitlement and delete the affected copies and registration
      materials. One copy of purchase and license records may be retained
      for legal compliance, without any right to execute the Software.
      Inaccessible routine backups may remain until ordinarily overwritten.

13.5. Termination does not affect accrued payment obligations, accrued
      claims, independently valid licenses, or rights under third-party
      open-source licenses. Provisions concerning ownership,
      confidentiality, disclaimers, liability, accrued obligations, and
      dispute resolution survive to the extent relevant.

